   "text": "roomba e5 wont charge properly, sometimes it does sometimes it doesnt"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Intermittent charging issues are very commonly caused by dirty or oxidised charging contacts on either the robot or the docking station. Before we consider a battery replacement, please unplug the dock and wipe the gold metal contact points on both the robot base and the dock pins with a dry cloth to remove any dust or grime. If they look clean and it still happens, let me know if you see any error lights flashing on the robot when it tries to charge."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok will try that. the app says Charging error 5 and it makes a two tone sound with a red ring when it fails"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "I can't help with Roomba robot vacuums as I only advise on standard UK domestic appliances like washing machines, fridges and ovens. For the Charging Error 5 on your E5, I recommend checking iRobot's official support site or contacting their customer service directly."
  }
